.TH POWEROFF 8
.SH NAME
poweroff, reboot, suspend \- turn the machine off, restart it, or sleep
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B poweroff
.br
.B reboot
.br
.B suspend
.RI [ n ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
These are commands built into the shell,
.BR sh (1),
for root. Each first commits the files, so nothing written is lost, then
goes through the ACPI server,
.BR acpid (4),
which tells the firmware (or the kernel alone where there is no acpid).
.TP
.B poweroff
Turn the machine off. The power button does the same.
.TP
.B reboot
Restart it.
.TP
.B suspend
Sleep (suspend to RAM, ACPI S3) until the power button or the lid wakes
the machine, or after
.I n
seconds (less than 3600: the clock's alarm). The device drivers start
again on waking; the desktop keeps its windows.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0, or 1 with a message: "not allowed" for a user, "not supported" on a
laptop without S3 (Modern Standby only).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR battery (1),
.BR acpid (4),
.BR intro (2),
.BR sh (1)
.SH BUGS
A sleep asked within 1 s of waking is not done ("just woke: not again").
No s2idle: laptops with only Modern Standby cannot sleep.
